## Observation boundary

PASS means no actual in-window unreadability, display collision or blank-media
failure was observed in the assigned screenshot windows. It does not approve a
whole media object or lesson. No mathematics, source, answer or figure-correctness
review was performed. Visible line crossings are described as rendered marks,
not evaluated as mathematical relationships.

Intentional horizontal-scroll remainders and top/bottom viewport fragments are
`OFF_WINDOW_NOT_OBSERVED`. They are neither inferred internal defects nor
approval of invisible tails. Empty padding or a caption/tail fragment alone
does not establish that an unseen media object is blank or correct.

All 11 figure-region rectangles in `result.json` are copied exactly from the
assignment, including fractional coordinates. They remain source-coordinate
rectangles, not estimated screenshot-coordinate boxes.

